sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-task-vm-upcloud-image-build.yaml, docs/reference/compute-drivers.md#build-the-upcloud-template and #sweep-upcloud, swamp/docs/task-vm-lifecycle.md (inline UpCloud curl on 209), docs/cli/README.md design rules R2-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 4 (no Gateway reads or progress writes from steps), 15 (no `admit` step; the Gateway computes every fixed agent envelope and host key), 3 (no in-run leftover sweep: the host sweep owns it), 1 and 19 (`delete-builder`, `delete-smoke` fold into the cleanup; one host key pair serves both servers), 6 (launch, boot and smoke checks one action per server; stop and templatize merge), 9 (one listing after the build feeds the end check and the cleanup), 18 (cleanup and prune as one forEach), 22 (curl on 209, guest actions as `@swamp/ssh exec` argv, Pi by `@swamp/ssh copy`).
  %% Kept: rules 14 and 16 do not apply to agent calls: `orbit-agent command` exits 0 and prints `{ok:false}` on a refusal, so each call keeps a typed reply check on 209. JSON answers of UpCloud need TypeScript, so `Read the template` and `Plan the cleanup` stay.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · UpCloud template build for a recipe
  %% kind: task_vm.upcloud_image_build
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane UC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane G icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant UC as UpCloud API<br/>HTTPS from 209
  participant G as Build servers<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit attempt 9<br/>UpCloud · task #5182
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `php artisan task-vms:build-upcloud-image`, `task-vms:build-recipe --retry` or `--rebuild`, or `RefreshUpCloudTaskVmBaseImage` when no verified template matches the deployed recipe
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - UpCloud is configured and no other UpCloud build runs; the ledger records attempt 9 before any remote work
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Gateway generates one ed25519 host key pair for the build servers and keeps it encrypted on the attempt
  %%> - at the run start it copies the UpCloud token and the private host key into the vault (R3), and refuses with `task_vm.image_build_superseded` when the recipe or agent pin changed
  %%> - the intent holds the recipe, identity, stamp, public host key, 209's SSH identity, the agent pin, every fixed agent envelope, the phase units and the templates pinned by live VMs
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>task-vm-upcloud-image-build
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `operation_id`, `node_id`, `kind`, the full public `intent`, and vault key names only: `task-vm-upcloud-token`, `task-vm-image-bootstrap-9`
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - every step on 209 (`labels: {role: swamp}`), not on the Gateway Node's worker (R4)
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no `admit` step and no key generation in the run (rules 15, 4)
  SW->>UC: Launch the builder<br/>POST /server · boot over ssh
  %%> How:
  %%> - child `task-vm-upcloud-image-server`: one inline `curl` on 209 reads the plans, TypeScript shapes the body, one `curl` posts it; the token and the private host key reach curl through `--variable`, never argv
  %%> - stock Ubuntu 26.04 template, builder user-data with the admitted host key, label `orbit-task-image=<stamp>`
  %%> - the create answer holds the UUID and the public IPv4 address
  %%> - pinned `@swamp/ssh exec` waits for the boot: OpenSSH `ConnectionAttempts` while sshd starts, then `cloud-init status --wait`, all under one literal timeout
  %%> - `@swamp/ssh copy` of 209's agent, `agent.install` against the pin, `guest.cloud-init`, `image.owner` for UID and GID 1000, `image.inspect-phase` for the boot id
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the server UUID and address, the boot id, and each phase's start and inspect envelope
  opt recipe pins a Pi build
    SW->>G: Stage the Pi build<br/>@swamp/ssh copy · sha256
    %%> How:
    %%> - child `task-vm-upcloud-image-pi`: copy the pinned binary from the Gateway Node to 209, `sha256sum -c` against its pin, copy it to the builder, then `sudo install` to `/var/cache/orbit/pi/<sha256>.bin`
    %%> Replaces:
    %%> - the chunked `pi.receive-artifact` transfer through the Gateway artifact callback
  end
  SW->>G: Run the phases<br/>start · wait · inspect
  %%> Phases:
  %%> - `apt-source`, `packages`, `javascript`, `rust`, `agent`, `pi`, in this order, as in the Incus build; `pi` runs only when the recipe pins a Pi build
  %%> How:
  %%> - child `task-vm-upcloud-image-phases`; each phase is `image.start-phase`, one `systemctl show --property=MainPID` read, `timeout 1500 tail --pid=PID -f /dev/null` (skipped when the phase already ended), and `image.inspect-phase`, which must report `complete` for the same boot id
  %%> - a failed phase stops the chain; no later phase starts
  SW->>G: Prepare and clean<br/>marker · verify · firewall · clean
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `image.recipe-marker`, `image.verify`, `image.boot`, `image.firewall` (ufw on, only `orbit:public-ssh-recovery` open), then `image.clean`, one at a time
  SW->>UC: Make the template<br/>stop · templatize
  %%> How:
  %%> - one soft stop with UpCloud's own 150-second hard-stop fallback, then the templatize request as `orbit-task-base-<stamp>-unverified`
  %%> - UpCloud refuses templatize until the server has stopped and changes nothing; curl's own bounded retry under one literal `timeout` is the wait (Q-WAIT), no script polls
  Note over SW: Read the template<br/>template_uuid
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - TypeScript on 209 reads the template UUID and title from the templatize answer
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the template UUID, which the Gateway reads from this step's output (rule 4)
  SW->>UC: Smoke the template<br/>launch from template · check
  %%> How:
  %%> - the same server child with the task VM user-data and the same host key; the create waits with curl's bounded retry while UpCloud still prepares the template
  %%> - boots as in step 3, then `image.verify` and `image.check` with the firewall check; the builder stays until the cleanup removes it
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a failed smoke check stops the build before promotion
  SW->>UC: Promote the template<br/>PUT title, labels
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - sets the `orbit.recipe` and `orbit-task-image` labels and renames the template to `orbit-task-base-<stamp>`; a PUT is safe to repeat, so curl retries while the smoke clone still holds the template
  SW->>UC: List servers, templates<br/>settle · always
  %%> When:
  %%> - after the build job, whatever its outcome, with the condition `always` (rule 19)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one listing of the servers labelled `orbit-task-image` and of the account's templates
  %%> Why:
  %%> - it finds this attempt's servers also when a create answer or a child's output was lost
  Note over SW: Plan the cleanup<br/>promoted · deletes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - TypeScript on 209 confirms the promoted title and labels, and picks what goes: this attempt's two servers; after promotion, verified templates beyond the two newest that no live VM pins; otherwise this attempt's unverified template
  Note over SW: Check the template<br/>assert
  %%> End check:
  %%> - after a successful build, the native `assert` checks that the listed promoted template is the one templatize made; this is the one end check (rule 9)
  SW->>UC: Delete servers, templates<br/>cleanup · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `forEach` over the plan; each started server gets a hard stop, then one `DELETE` with its storage, which curl retries while UpCloud still stops it (Q-WAIT)
  %%> - it replaces the separate `delete-builder`, `delete-smoke` and `prune` steps (rules 1, 18)
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - best effort with `allowFailure` (rule 10): the run's outcome stays, and the next host sweep removes what stays
  alt template promoted
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>template_uuid
    Note over GW: Record attempt 9<br/>succeeded · template verified
    %%> Result:
    %%> - new UpCloud claims for this recipe use the template
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark attempt 9 failed<br/>previous template stays
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a refused agent reply keeps its own code; reconcile alerts for the identity; `task-vms:build-recipe --retry` records a new attempt
  end
